  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ELF - Mfalme Productions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gender inequality and inequity remains a persistent problem across Kenya&apos;s cultural, corporate and political spheres. Despite significant policy adjustments that seek to redefine the role of women in society, their participation and visibility remains low. This has often been attributed to deep seated socio-economic structures that have confined women to the fringes of leadership and political participation. New media offers a medium through which this can be rectified by enabling women who have broken social barriers to share their experiences with their peers. This project seeks to avail an opportunity for this powerful dialogue by adding the voice of women to the popular Makarao animation series produced by Mfalme Productions. It combines traditional and new media technologies to deliver a message of freedom and empowerment to a diverse audience while transferring relevant skills to content creators with a demonstrated passion for digital storytelling.

Mfalme&apos;s multi-stakeholder approach is designed to bridge the growing digital dividebetween the different genders and socio-cultural groups across Kenya. By leveraging KBC TV&apos;s nationwide reach, we hope to empower individuals and communities in the farthest reaches of the country with the same information reaching urban Kenyans on social media platforms. The project&apos;s training element also aims to equip young journalists with digital content creation skills to enable them produce high impact audio-visual content for today&apos;s mobile-first audiences.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emerging Leaders Foundation (ELF)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Emerging Leaders Foundation Africa (ELF-Africa) exists to empower, support and accompany young women and men to achieve meaningful, dignified and impactful participation in governance, economy and public affairs at all levels of society anchored on the foundational values-based approach to leadership as service. Emerging leaders Foundation is a platform that nurtures, grows and equips leaders to sustainable change in their communities. At ELF, the approach is to equip young people with knowledge and skills to not justprepare them for the future but to support them to create the future they want to see through capacity building, experiential learning, mentorship &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; coaching, Advocacy &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Lobbying as well as policy dialogue. ELF has steadily worked towards realizing dignified societies with values-based leaders by imparting over 7000 and over 200,000 youth directly and indirectly across Kenya with larger representation of young women.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
